// Counted-loop flattening rule. `(repeat body count step)` is a loop that runs
// `body` `count` times. The single rule says a count-1 loop is just its body.
//
// It is load-bearing for the live-vs-at-start divergence: with
// `--only-use-dsrs-at-start`, each program's min-term is extracted up front, and
// this rule flattens a count-1 loop to its bare body — so the loop skeleton is
// gone before abstraction search even starts, and a count-parameterized loop
// abstraction can no longer match that program. Live search keeps both forms in
// the same e-class, so it can still roll the loop across the count-1 site.
rep_1: (repeat ?x 1 ?n) => ?x
